{
	"__schema" : "4.1",
	"__type" : "page",
	"children" : {
		"__type" : "snippets",
		"items" : [
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:30:20.138462+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:43:33.833059+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "wtYaaF0STg+TB6sZuga4Rw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "With Pharo's {{gtClass:SubscriptionRegistry}}, an announcer that has both strong and weak subscribers can keep its strong subscribers alive for as long as some other weak subscriber lives, and unsubscribing does not stop the leak. {{gtClass:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry}} is a registry an announcer can use instead, in which this cannot happen. This page explains the leak and how the mixed registry avoids it; the leak itself is explored in more detail on the Glamorous Toolkit Book page [[Exploring memory leaks when mixing weak and strong subscriptions in announcers]]."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:43:06.074103+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:43:42.104935+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "A5YOOo7WTG2nyOnK8/QStA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "An **ephemeron** is a key/value pair whose value is kept alive only while its key is reachable from somewhere else; in Pharo it is a {{gtClass:WeakKeyAssociation}}. When nothing else references the key any more, the garbage collector *fires* the ephemeron, and shortly after the collection the finalization process *mourns* it, which runs its cleanup."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:44:01.474623+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:44:01.474623+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "6GpC8dixSU6yJddrNvhEKQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "A **strong** subscription ({{gtClass:AnnouncementSubscription}}) references its subscriber, so the announcer keeps the subscriber alive. A **weak** subscription ({{gtClass:WeakAnnouncementSubscription}}) holds its subscriber in a weak slot, and to learn when the subscriber dies it registers an ephemeron in the global {{gtClass:FinalizationRegistry}} ({{gtMethod:WeakAnnouncementSubscription>>#register}}): key the subscriber, value the subscription. The subscription references its **announcer** strongly, because {{gtMethod:WeakAnnouncementSubscription>>#finalize}} needs it."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:44:28.455188+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:44:28.455188+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "XOwoe51cTaS2KrqkryGcDA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "While a weak subscriber Y lives, its global ephemeron keeps its subscription alive, and with it the announcer and everything subscribed **strongly** to that announcer:\n\n{{gtClass:FinalizationRegistry}} {{gtMethod:FinalizationRegistry class>>#default|label=#selector}} → ephemeron (key Y, alive) → weak subscription of Y → announcer → registry → strong subscription → X"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:44:38.683178+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:44:38.683178+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "YtUEoffAQpC1ilPy7fuMzQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The typical case: a graphical element holds its model and subscribes strongly to the model's announcer, while some other long-lived object subscribes weakly to the same announcer. Model and element then stay alive as long as that other object does:\n\n{{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#elementOfModelLeaksWithPlainRegistry|expanded}}\n\n"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:44:40.414018+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:44:40.414018+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "qrIn8N52SPquxYxE6YdQGw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "Two cases do not leak a subscriber:\n\n- **The same object subscribed both strongly and weakly** does not leak by itself: the only path to it starts at its own ephemeron, and an ephemeron does not keep its key alive.\n- **An announcer with only weak subscriptions** does not keep its subscribers alive, but a live weak subscriber still keeps the announcer itself and its registry alive."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:30:20.138535+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:44:40.417669+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "Q3fMn4b5SUyLmZ/vO5Yemw=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The leak needs a strong subscription plus a weak subscription of a **different**, longer-lived object.\n\n**Weak block subscriptions are not weak.** A {{gtClass:SubscriptionRegistry}} holds a weak subscription strongly, and the subscription holds its action strongly. A block passed to {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#weak|label=#selector}} {{gtMethod:WeakSubscriptionBuilder>>#when:do:for:|label=#selector}} that refers to its subscriber therefore keeps the subscriber alive as long as the announcer lives; Pharo's own {{gtMethod:WeakSubscriptionBuilder>>#when:do:for:}} warns about this.\n\nThe subscription graphs of {{gtClass:GtAnnouncerGraphExamples}} draw these chains for each case, with a plain and with a mixed registry."
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:43:00.076691+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:43:00.076691+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "hihQbpcESqmEJ6DOat7NRA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# The leak with Pharo's registries"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:30:20.138576+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:00.585068+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "aUiwau8SQMG2ut223BGOtQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "The global entry is removed only when the subscriber dies. {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#unsubscribe:|label=#selector}} sends {{gtMethod:WeakAnnouncementSubscription>>#unregister}}, which in GT does nothing while {{gtMethod:GtWeakSubscriptionDisableFinalizationFlag class>>#isEnabled}} answers true (the default); the real removal, {{gtMethod:FinalizationRegistry>>#remove:ifAbsent:}}, would scan all entries and remove the first one with that key. {{gtMethod:Announcer>>#removeSubscription:|label=#selector}} never unregisters. So an unsubscribed weak subscription keeps its entry, and the entry keeps the announcer reachable, until the subscriber dies. An element that is added to and removed from the scene several times collects one stale entry per subscription each time. In one GT image, 98,419 of 223,386 global entries for weak subscriptions (44 %) belonged to subscriptions that were no longer in their announcer, most of them from Bloc text elements and editors."
						}
					]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:00.581305+01:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:00.581305+01:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "DXDosKkvSEqXSiPh58Pvlg=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "# Unsubscribing does not help"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:31.133596+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:31.133596+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "XbueRRNBRqe3eG81gXyyow=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "{{gtClass:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistry}} keeps strong subscriptions as before, but stores weak subscriptions ({{gtClass:GtEphemeronAnnouncementSubscription}}) itself: for each weak subscriber it holds one ephemeron, keyed on the subscriber, whose value is the set of that subscriber's subscriptions. Nothing global references these ephemerons; the only path to them goes through the announcer."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:34.499755+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:34.499755+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "4cuh7vGTRx65cSZyx8helg=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "- **A live weak subscriber no longer keeps the announcer alive.** There is no chain from a global root to the announcer, so the element and its model from the example above are collected while the other weak subscriber lives. Compare {{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#elementOfModelLeaksWithPlainRegistry}} with:\n\n{{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#elementOfModelIsCollectedDespiteLiveWeakSubscriber|expanded}}\n"
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:37.563114+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:37.563114+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "WBgk/dJvRMOXlstQ0V9NAA=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "- **Unsubscribing removes everything.** The subscriber's entry, with its ephemeron, leaves the registry; nothing stays behind anywhere ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#unsubscribedWeakSubscriberDoesNotKeepElementAlive}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:38.981208+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:38.981208+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "KwUMBVh3TS2nA2UYXOb8DQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "- **A dead weak subscriber is removed by the registry itself.** When the subscriber is collected, the VM fires its ephemeron and the registry drops the whole group ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#weakSubscriberIsGarbageCollected}}). An announcer that is no longer used is simply garbage, ephemerons included ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#announcerIsCollectedWhileWeakSubscriberLives}})."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"createEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"createTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:40.203142+01:00"
								}
							},
							"editEmail" : {
								"__type" : "email",
								"emailString" : "<unknown>"
							},
							"editTime" : {
								"__type" : "time",
								"time" : {
									"__type" : "dateAndTime",
									"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-11-22T16:45:40.203142+01:00"
								}
							},
							"uid" : {
								"__type" : "uid",
								"uidString" : "9oduDBciRVOF+ddVUTLmYQ=="
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "- **Weak block subscriptions are weak.** A block that refers to its subscriber sits in the value of the subscriber's ephemeron, which does not keep the subscriber alive ({{gtMethod:GtMixedSubscriptionRegistryExamples>>#weakSubscriberCapturedByItsBlockIsCollected}})."
						},
						{
